{"name":"Kiwi","hex":"#749e4e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Kiwi","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A native or inhabitant of New Zealand; a New Zealander."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of, from or relating to New Zealand."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Kiwi"}],"entries":[{"title":"Kiwi (bird)","blocks":[{"text":"Kiwi are flightless birds endemic to New Zealand of the order Apterygiformes. The five extant species fall into the family Apterygidae and genus Apteryx. Approximately the size of a domestic chicken, kiwi are the smallest ratites."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/TeTuatahianui.jpg/330px-TeTuatahianui.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kiwi_(bird)","wikidata":"Q43642"},{"title":"Kiwi (nickname)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Kiwi\" is a common self-reference used by New Zealanders, though it is also used internationally. The label is generally viewed as a symbol of pride and affection for most people of New Zealand, however there are New Zealanders, particularly some with Māori heritage, that find the appellation jarring and prefer not to identify with it."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Kiwi_holding_kiwi.jpg/330px-Kiwi_holding_kiwi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kiwi_(nickname)","wikidata":"Q2552898"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Am_media-v-602297.jpg/500px-Am_media-v-602297.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Am_media-v-602297.jpg/1280px-Am_media-v-602297.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Am_media-v-602297.jpg/500px-Am_medi